    ],
    "reading_order": 3,
    "text": "Let us now find the distance between any two\npoints P(x1, y1) and Q(x2, y2). Draw PR and QS\nperpendicular to the x-axis. A perpendicular from the\npoint P on QS is drawn to meet it at the point\nT (see Fig. 7.5).",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH107",
    "page": 4,
    "block_id": "jemh107_p004_b04",
    "type": "formula",
    "bbox": [
      48.0,
      170.13,
      278.27,
      184.99
    ],
    "reading_order": 4,
    "text": "Then,\nOR = x1, OS = x2.\nSo, RS = x2 – x1 = PT.",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH107",
    "page": 4,
    "block_id": "jemh107_p004_b05",
    "type": "figure",
    "bbox": [
